# Content to Campaign bridge: what a CONSUMING app needs.
#
# This is the whole set. Two values, one of them a secret. Copy into the AiCoE
# app environment and fill the blank.
#
# Nothing here grants write access: every endpoint the dashboard needs is a
# read, and the token is a shared secret for the bridge as a whole, not a
# per-user credential. Treat it as a service credential and keep it server
# side. Do not ship it to a browser.

# ── Where the bridge is ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
C2C_BRIDGE_URL=https://c2c-agent-bridge.onrender.com
# Local bridge instead:
# C2C_BRIDGE_URL=http://localhost:8787

# ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FILL THIS IN. Sent as: Authorization: Bearer <value>
#
# Where to get it: Render dashboard, c2c-agent-bridge service, Environment tab,
# BRIDGE_API_TOKEN. The deploy blueprint generates it, so copy the existing
# value rather than setting a new one; changing it breaks the studio, which
# holds the same value as VITE_LIVE_TOKEN on Vercel.
#
# Every /api route except /api/health requires it. A missing or wrong token is
# a 401, never a 404, so you can tell "wrong path" from "wrong key".
C2C_BRIDGE_TOKEN=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only used to attribute assistant conversations in the transcript. It is NOT
# authentication and NOT authorisation: the bridge does not check it.
# C2C_ACTOR_ID=you@levelshift.com
